ang="EN">MANGANESE-ZINC FERRITE AND METHOD FOR PRODUCING THE SAME</invention-title> <invention-title load-source="docdb" status="new" lang="FR">FERRITE DE MANGANESE-ZINC ET PROCEDE DE PRODUCTION</invention-title> <citations><patent-citations><patcit ucid="JP-61117804-A" status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>61117804</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X"  name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-6204025-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>6204025</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1030318A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE SHOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TDK CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, SHOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TDK CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE SHOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, SHOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A manganese-zinc ferrite having a high initial permeability in a wide band, especially an especially high initial permeability in a low-frequency region of about 10 kHz and a method for producing the same. The method including a main temperature maintaining step of maintaining the temperature at 1200 DEG  to 1450  DEG C during baking is characterized in that before the main temperature maintaining step the method includes an in-baking temperature decreasing step in which the lowest temperature is in the range from 1000 DEG  to 1400  DEG C which is 50  DEG C or more lower than the temperature maintained in the main temperature maintaining step. The thus produced manganese-zinc ferrite contains as main components 50 to 56 mol% of iron oxide in terms of Fe2O3, 22 to 39 mol% of manganese oxide in terms of MnO, and 8 to 25 mol% of zinc oxide in terms of ZnO and has an average grain size of 50 to 150  mu m.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une ferrite de manganèse-zinc présentant une trés forte perméabilité initiale dans une large bande, et en particulier, dans une zone basse fréquence d'environ 10 kHz et un procédé de production de cette ferrite. Ce procédé comprend une étape principale consistant à maintenir la température entre 1200 et 1450  DEG C pendant la cuisson, et une étape de réduction de la température durant la cuisson,au cours de laquelle la plus faible température est comprise entre 1000 et 1400  DEG C. Cette dernière température correspond à au moins 50  DEG C de moins que la température observée pendant l'étape principale. La ferrite de manganèse-zinc ainsi produite contient comme composants principaux de 50 à 56 % mol. d'oxyde de fer en termes de Fe2O3, de 22 à 39 % mol. d'oxyde de manganèse en termes de MnO et de 8 à 25 % mol. d'oxyde de zinc en termes de ZnO. En outre, la ferrite selon l'invention présente une granulométrie moyenne de 50 à 150  mu m.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>